cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Tourism service supply chains in ten emerging economies:
  data collection, audited analysis and validation notebooks
message: >-
  If you use this software or the accompanying materials, please
  cite both the archived release and the associated article.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Douglas
    family-names: De Souza Rodrigues
    email: rodriguesdouglas@id.uff.br
    affiliation: >-
      Production Engineering Department, Fluminense Federal
      University, Petropolis, RJ, Brazil
    orcid: 'https://orcid.org/0000-0001-7473-7425'
repository-code: 'https://github.com/douglaskorvo/tourism_supply_chain'
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.22289163
abstract: >-
  Versioned notebooks and aggregate reference outputs documenting the
  retrieval and audited analysis of a tourism-review corpus for a study
  of reported disruption exposure and customer impact in tourism service
  supply chains across ten emerging economies. This version also deposits the
  held-out validation procedure: sampling of the double-coded review set, the
  agreement statistics computed on returned codings, the provider query-stratum
  face-validity audit, and a provider-grouped gold-labelled split. No review-level
  platform content, human-coding record or validation metric is redistributed.
keywords:
  - tourism service supply chain
  - reported disruption
  - customer impact
  - user-generated content
  - dictionary-based content analysis
  - held-out validation
  - inter-rater reliability
  - rare-events logistic regression
  - equivalence testing
  - reproducibility
  - emerging economies
